{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"16907fe07c4bb266d28d66d5996b9f9dfe9a0d925dbb68ba0e09c89b36b5cb0d","digest":{"component_or_area":"test infrastructure / conftest","key_entities":["_rebar_repo_template","tests/interfaces/conftest.py","rebar.list_tickets()","rebar.init_repo()","pytest.MonkeyPatch.context()","test_template_stays_virgin","tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py"],"problem_keywords":["fixture assertion","test isolation","template invariant","virgin state validation"],"propositions":["The template fixture _rebar_repo_template asserts only .rebar absence but does not assert no tickets exist in the template build.","A test-level assertion in test_template_stays_virgin alone leaves narrowed pytest runs (e.g. pytest tests/interfaces/store) unprotected because that test is not selected.","The missing assertion must live inside the MonkeyPatch.context() block where REBAR_ROOT and cwd are pinned so that rebar.list_tickets() can be called reliably against the template.","Pre-warming the template with tickets would silently invert session-log count assertions in dependent tests unless the no-tickets invariant is enforced at fixture construction."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787891693493461001,"uuid":"1603d389-9eb0-4f23-bc1f-c385d380383c"}